  "title": "Materion's aluminum-scandium sputtering targets power RF, mobile and broadband devices",
  "summary": "Aluminum-scandium (AlSc) alloys are lightweight metal alloys first widely used in the aerospace industry. More recently, high-scandium-content AlSc targets have gained prominence in semiconductor manufacturing, where they can be sputtered reactively with nitrogen to produce piezoelectric AlScN layers.",
